== Awards and nominations ==
{{main|List of awards and nominations received by James Burrows}}

Over the course of his career, Burrows was nominated for fifteen [[Directors Guild of America]] awards, and for an [[Emmy Award]] every year between 1980 and 2005, excluding 1997.<ref name="Variety Feted by Academy">{{cite news|last1=Tepper|first1=Allegra|title=Director James Burrows Feted by TV Academy|url=http://variety.com/2013/tv/news/jennifer-aniston-tv-academy-celebrate-james-burrows-1200704682/|access-date=17 July 2015|work=Variety|date=8 October 2013|ref=Variety|archive-date=22 July 2015|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150722053528/http://variety.com/2013/tv/news/jennifer-aniston-tv-academy-celebrate-james-burrows-1200704682/|url-status=live}}</ref> Burrows won 11 [[Emmy Awards]] and five [[Directors Guild of America Award]]s.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.televisionacademy.com/bios/james-burrows|title=James Burrows|website=Television Academy|access-date=2026-06-20|archive-date=2026-06-19|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260619211446/https://www.televisionacademy.com/bios/james-burrows|url-status=live}}</ref> The [[Academy of Television Arts and Sciences]] celebrated Burrows' forty-year career by hosting a panel in his honor on October 7, 2013.<ref name="Variety Feted by Academy" />

